:"output_text","text":"I’ll add the read-only task directory using the existing filter rules, then test filter intersections, ordering, and persistence.\n","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"commentary"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_019b8838198d3241016acd32a4b34487d1ad26bdf1011b6c19","call_id":"call_782c270f34594e5e8885edadefea5d23","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"const listTasks = db.prepare('SELECT id, title, completed, priority, due_date, notes, deleted FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ? ORDER BY position ASC, id ASC');\",\"newText\":\"const listTasks = db.prepare('SELECT id, title, completed, priority, due_date, notes, deleted FROM tasks WHERE project_id = ? ORDER BY position ASC, id ASC');\\nconst listDirectoryTasks = db.prepare(`\\n  SELECT t.*, p.name AS project_name FROM projects p JOIN tasks t ON t.project_id = p.id\\n  WHERE p.archived = ? ORDER BY p.id ASC, t.position ASC, t.id ASC\\n`);\"},{\"oldText\":\"    <h1>Workboard</h1>\\n\",\"newText\":\"    <h1>Workboard</h1>\\n    <form method=\\\"get\\\" action=\\\"/directory\\\"><button type=\\\"submit\\\">Task directory</button></form>\\n\"},{\"oldText\":\"function renderProjectPage(project, filter = 'All', error = '', priorityFilter = 'All', range = emptyRange, draft = range, query = '') {\",\"newText\":\"function matchesTask(task, filter, priorityFilter, range, query) {\\n  return matchesSearch(task.title, query) &&\\n    (filter === 'Deleted' ? Boolean(task.deleted) : !task.deleted &&\\n      (filter === 'All' || Boolean(task.completed) === (filter === 'Completed'))) &&\\n    (priorityFilter === 'All' || task.priority === priorityFilter) &&\\n    ((!range.from && !range.through) || (task.due_date &&\\n      (!range.from || task.due_date >= range.from) &&\\n      (!range.through || task.due_date <= range.through)));\\n}\\n\\nfunction directoryPage(scope, filter, priorityFilter, range, query, error = '', draft = range) {\\n  const tasks = listDirectoryTasks.all(scope === 'Archived' ? 1 : 0)\\n    .filter(task => matchesTask(task, filter, priorityFilter, range, query));\\n  const filterFields = `<input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"scope\\\" value=\\\"${scope}\\\">\\n    <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"filter\\\" value=\\\"${filter}\\\">\\n    <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"priorityFilter\\\" value=\\\"${priorityFilter}\\\">`;\\n  const rangeFields = `<input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"dueFrom\\\" value=\\\"${escapeHtml(range.from)}\\\">\\n    <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"dueThrough\\\" value=\\\"${escapeHtml(range.through)}\\\">`;\\n  const options = (values, selected) => values.map(value =>\\n    `<option${value === selected ? ' selected' : ''}>${value}</option>`).join('');\\n  return page('Task directory', `\\n    <h1>Task directory</h1>\\n    <form method=\\\"get\\\" action=\\\"/\\\"><button type=\\\"submit\\\">Projects</button></form>\\n    ${error ? `<div role=\\\"alert\\\">${escapeHtml(error)}</div>` : ''}\\n    <form method=\\\"get\\\" action=\\\"/directory\\\">\\n      ${searchField(query)}${rangeFields}\\n      <label for=\\\"project-scope\\\">Project scope</label>\\n      <select id=\\\"project-scope\\\" name=\\\"scope\\\" onchange=\\\"this.form.submit()\\\">${options(['Active', 'Archived'], scope)}</select>\\n      <label for=\\\"directory-task-filter\\\">Task filter</label>\\n      <select id=\\\"directory-task-filter\\\" name=\\\"filter\\\" onchange=\\\"this.form.submit()\\\">${options(taskFilters, filter)}</select>\\n      <label for=\\\"directory-priority-filter\\\">Priority filter</label>\\n      <select id=\\\"directory-priority-filter\\\" name=\\\"priorityFilter\\\" onchange=\\\"this.form.submit()\\\">${options(['All', ...priorities], priorityFilter)}</select>\\n    </form>\\n    <form method=\\\"get\\\" action=\\\"/directory\\\">\\n      ${filterFields}${rangeFields}\\n      <label for=\\\"directory-search\\\">Directory search</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"directory-search\\\" type=\\\"text\\\" name=\\\"search\\\" value=\\\"${escapeHtml(query)}\\\">\\n      <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Search directory</button>\\n    </form>\\n    <form method=\\\"get\\\" action=\\\"/directory/due-range\\\">\\n      ${filterFields}${searchField(query)}\\n      <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"appliedFrom\\\" value=\\\"${escapeHtml(range.from)}\\\">\\n      <input type=\\\"hidden\\\" name=\\\"appliedThrough\\\" value=\\\"${escapeHtml(range.through)}\\\">\\n      <label for=\\\"directory-due-from\\\">Due from</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"directory-due-from\\\" type=\\\"text\\\" name=\\\"dueFrom\\\" value=\\\"${escapeHtml(draft.from)}\\\">\\n      <label for=\\\"directory-due-through\\\">Due through</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"directory-due-through\\\" type=\\\"text\\\" name=\\\"dueThrough\\\" value=\\\"${escapeHtml(draft.through)}\\\">\\n      <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Apply due range</button>\\n    </form>\\n    ${tasks.length ? tasks.map(task => `\\n      <div class=\\\"row\\\" data-testid=\\\"directory-task-row\\\">\\n        <span data-testid=\\\"directory-task-title\\\" style=\\\"white-space: pre-wrap\\\">${escapeHtml(task.title)}</span>\\n        <span data-testid=\\\"directory-project-name\\\" style=\\\"white-space: pre-wrap\\\">${escapeHtml(task.project_name)}</span>\\n        <span data-testid=\\\"directory-task-completion\\\">${task.completed ? 'Completed' : 'Open'}</span>\\n        <span data-testid=\\\"directory-task-priority\\\">${escapeHtml(task.priority)}</span>\\n        <span data-testid=\\\"directory-task-due-date\\\">${escapeHtml(task.due_date)}</span>\\n        <span data-testid=\\\"directory-task-notes\\\" style=\\\"white-space: pre-wrap\\\">${escapeHtml(task.notes)}</span>\\n        <form method=\\\"get\\\" action=\\\"/projects/${task.project_id}\\\"><button type=\\\"submit\\\">Open project</button></form>\\n      </div>`).join('') : '<p>No matching tasks.</p>'}\\n  `);\\n}\\n\\nfunction renderProjectPage(project, filter = 'All', error = '', priorityFilter = 'All', range = emptyRange, draft = range, query = '') {\"},{\"oldText\":\"  const tasks = listTasks.all(project.id).filter(task =>\\n    matchesSearch(task.title, query) &&\\n    (filter === 'Deleted' ? Boolean(task.deleted) : !task.deleted &&\\n      (filter === 'All' || Boolean(task.completed) === (filter === 'Completed'))) &&\\n    (priorityFilter === 'All' || task.priority === priorityFilter) &&\\n    ((!range.from && !range.through) || (task.due_date &&\\n      (!range.from || task.due_date >= range.from) &&\\n      (!range.through || task.due_date <= range.through))));\",\"newText\":\"  const tasks = listTasks.all(project.id).filter(task => matchesTask(task, filter, priorityFilter, range, query));\"},{\"oldText\":\"    } else if (req.method === 'GET' && path === '/') {\",\"newText\":\"    } else if (req.method === 'GET' && (path === '/directory' || path === '/directory/due-range')) {\\n      const params = url.searchParams;\\n      const scope = validProjectFilter(params.get('scope'));\\n      const filter = validFilter(params.get('filter'));\\n      const priorityFilter = validPriorityFilter(params.get('priorityFilter'));\\n      const draft = { from: (params.get('dueFrom') || '').trim(), through: (params.get('dueThrough') || '').trim() };\\n      const error = path === '/directory/due-range' ? rangeError(draft) : '';\\n      const range = error ? readRange(params, 'applied') : appliedRange;\\n      html(res, error ? 422 : 200, directoryPage(scope, filter, priorityFilter, range, appliedQuery, error, error ? draft : range));\\n    } else if (req.method === 'GET' && path === '/') {\"}]}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","offset","limit"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},{"type":"null"}]},"limit":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command","timeout"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"},{"type":"null"}]}},"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":true},{"type":"function","name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"t